<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">II </span><span id="S2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">System Model</span></h2>

<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">II-A</span> </span><span id="S2.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Overall System Architecture</span></h3>

<figure id="S2.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.13634v1/system_architecture.png" id="S2.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:229/141;" width="229" height="141" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 1</span>: </span><span id="S2.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The proposed zkFed-enabled UAV-assisted FL system architecture.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our proposed DT-assisted zkFed framework for UAV-enabled privacy-preserving FL is illustrated in Fig. <a href="#S2.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ II-A Overall System Architecture ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. The system integrates UAVs, FL agents (user devices), and a DT layer to enhance energy efficiency, optimize resource allocation, and ensure robust privacy and security. The UAVs function as aerial FL aggregators, dynamically adjusting their flight trajectories, transmission power, and user association strategies to maintain efficient communication and resource allocation. We consider a UAV assisted FL system with <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> user devices, denoted as <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}=\{1,2,...,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}=\{1,2,...,N\}</annotation></semantics></math>, each of which possesses a private dataset <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. The system operates over <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> global communication rounds, with each device training its local model using dataset <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and uploading encrypted model parameters to a UAV based aggregator. Given the inherent constraints of UAV assisted networks, including limited energy capacity, dynamic mobility, and constrained communication resources, we employ a DT model to enable real-time optimization of computational efficiency and network performance.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The overall interactions between UAVs, the DT framework, and zkFed-based FL can be summarized as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="S2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">User devices: The user devices (edge clients) are responsible for performing local FL model training on their private datasets <math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. To ensure energy-efficient training, they utilize computation resources, specifically CPU cycles, to optimize processing rates. Once the training is completed, the encrypted model updates are transmitted to UAVs for aggregation using frequency-domain multiple access (FDMA). Additionally, these user devices serve as digital replicas in the DT layer, enabling real-time performance evaluation and optimization.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">UAV aggregators: UAVs act as mobile FL coordinators, dynamically adjusting their trajectory, transmit power, and computation allocation to optimize communication and learning efficiency. They utilize adaptive energy-aware scheduling to balance FL model training with UAV operational constraints, ensuring optimal resource utilization. To enhance security and privacy, UAVs implement zkFed, enabling the verification of encrypted model updates without exposing sensitive data. Furthermore, they maintain bidirectional communication with the DT layer, receiving optimized flight trajectories and system control recommendations to improve overall system performance.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">DT layer: The DT layer constructs virtual models of UAVs and user devices, enabling the simulation of real-time system performance. It provides predictive optimization for UAV trajectory planning, resource allocation, and energy consumption, ensuring efficient operations. Additionally, the DT layer continuously analyzes communication latencies, processing delays, and security vulnerabilities, refining FL operations to enhance overall system reliability and security.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Zero-Knowledge Proof for Federated Learning (zkFed):
By having clients train local models using local data and then submit those models to the server rather than the raw data, FL systems seek to protect client privacy. The server then combines these local models to provide an updated global model. FL systems typically involve a central server that, while generally trustworthy, operates under an <span id="S2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">“honest-but-curious”</span> model where it can access all client data. To improve privacy, these systems can incorporate techniques like adding noise to the data <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>. Despite the advanced features of FL frameworks, clients must trust that the server accurately aggregates the data. However, this aggregation is often opaque, posing risks such as the potential for a global aggregation attack. In such scenarios, the server might not utilize all client data to reduce computational demands or unfairly prioritize some client models over others <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In our framework, the DT layer maintains synchronization with the physical UAV–user network through continuous telemetry and computation-status updates. Each UAV is equipped with a GPS receiver and inertial sensors for real-time position and motion tracking, along with wireless link-quality estimators to monitor channel gain as expressed in <a href="#S2.E3" title="In II-B Physical System Model ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. Ground user devices periodically report their current computation frequency, residual energy, and training status, which are represented in the physical model by parameters such as <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{\mathrm{train}}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">train</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{\mathrm{train}}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\mathrm{train}}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">train</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\mathrm{train}}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. These measurements are transmitted to the DT server via the existing UAV–ground FDMA links and relayed over the UAV–cloud backhaul using lightweight IoT messaging protocols to minimize overhead. UAV telemetry and channel-state information are refreshed every 1–2 seconds, while aggregated user computation and energy metrics are updated every 5 seconds. Upon receiving these updates, the DT layer refreshes the virtual replica of the network and executes optimization routines to adjust UAV trajectory <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x[k],y[k])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x[k],y[k])</annotation></semantics></math>, transmission powers <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\mathrm{UAV}}[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">UAV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\mathrm{UAV}}[k]</annotation></semantics></math>, and user scheduling. The optimized control parameters are then returned to the UAV with an end-to-end feedback delay of less than 200 ms, allowing DT-driven adjustments to be applied within the same global FL round.</span> Each FL round consists of four key stages, as illustrated in Fig. <a href="#S2.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ II-A Overall System Architecture ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>:</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS1.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">II-A</span>1 </span>Local model training and DT-optimized computation scheduling</h4>

<div id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each user performs local FL model training using dataset <math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and optimizes its processing rate (<math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>) to minimize energy consumption. The DT layer simulates user computational loads, predicting energy consumption and scheduling adjustments. To reduce communication latency, UAVs dynamically allocate bandwidth (<math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>) and transmit power (<math id="S2.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>) to ensure reliable model updates.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS1.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">II-A</span>2 </span>UAV-assisted model aggregation and zkFed verification</h4>

<div id="S2.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After local training, user devices encrypt their model parameters using homomorphic encryption and transmit them to the UAV using frequency-domain multiple access (FDMA). The UAV aggregates these encrypted models using a privacy-preserving zkFed scheme, verifying each update via zero-knowledge proofs (ZKPs). The DT layer continuously monitors UAV trajectory adjustments, ensuring optimal positioning for minimal transmission delays.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS1.SSS3.6" class="ltx_text">II-A</span>3 </span>Global model update and secure zk-SNARK validation</h4>

<div id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The UAV updates the global FL model by aggregating verified encrypted updates. A zk-SNARK proof is generated, allowing devices to verify the validity of the global model without revealing the underlying computations. The DT simultaneously recomputes UAV trajectory optimizations, dynamically adjusting flight paths based on real-time user density and communication constraints.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS1.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS1.SSS4.6" class="ltx_text">II-A</span>4 </span>Model distribution and next iteration</h4>

<div id="S2.SS1.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The UAV broadcasts the updated global model to all user devices. Users validate the model using zkFed-based authentication mechanisms, ensuring the integrity of the training process. The DT continuously optimizes energy allocation, trajectory adjustments, and user scheduling to improve efficiency in the subsequent learning round.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">II-B</span> </span><span id="S2.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Physical System Model</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider a DT-assisted FL framework where a single UAV works as an aerial aggregator to collaborate with a group of terrestrial users (denoted as by <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}=\{1,2,\ldots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}=\{1,2,\ldots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math>) within its operational range. It is assumed the UAV’s position is denoted as (<math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x[k],y[k],H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x[k],y[k],H</annotation></semantics></math>). the user <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>’s position is denoted as <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[x^{E}_{\textit{n}},y^{E}_{\textit{n}},0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mi>E</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[x^{E}_{\textit{n}},y^{E}_{\textit{n}},0]</annotation></semantics></math>. The UAV is assumed to fly at a fixed altitude <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> above ground, which is considered the minimum height necessary to avoid obstacles.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The UAV’s operation time can be partitioned into small time slots in the operational time span <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> into <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> equal intervals, resulting in <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=K\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=K\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> implies the duration of each interval. This segmentation granularity allows us to treat the UAV’s position as stable within each interval, denoted by (<math id="S2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x[k],Y[k],H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x[k],Y[k],H</annotation></semantics></math>). The UAV’s horizontal trajectory (<math id="S2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t),y(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t),y(t)</annotation></semantics></math>) across <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> can be succinctly represented by the sequence <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x[k],y[k]\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x[k],y[k]\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given the UAV’s maximum velocity <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\textit{max}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\textit{max}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, its traversal distance per interval stands at <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=v_{\textit{max}}\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=v_{\textit{max}}\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The UAV’s initial and final positions, defined as (<math id="S2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0},y_{0},H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0},y_{0},H</annotation></semantics></math>) and (<math id="S2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{F},y_{F},H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{F},y_{F},H</annotation></semantics></math>) respectively, align with mission directives. As such, the UAV’s navigational constraints are articulated as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E1.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(x[1]-x_{0})^{2}+(y[1]-y_{0})^{2}\leq L^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(x[1]-x_{0})^{2}+(y[1]-y_{0})^{2}\leq L^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E1.x1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1.x1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(x[k+1]-x[k])^{2}+(y[k+1]-y[k])^{2}\leq L^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(x[k+1]-x[k])^{2}+(y[k+1]-y[k])^{2}\leq L^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E1.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad k=1,\ldots,K-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad k=1,\ldots,K-1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1b)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E1.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(x_{F}-x[K])^{2}+(y_{F}-y[K])^{2}\leq L^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(x_{F}-x[K])^{2}+(y_{F}-y[K])^{2}\leq L^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1c)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Within this framework, the UAV assumes the role of a parameter server, facilitating each user <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> in training a FL model using their unique local dataset <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\textit{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\textit{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which collectively enriches the overarching dataset <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>. Comprising input-output pairs <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(\mathbf{v}_{\textit{n}},z_{\textit{n}})\}_{i=1}^{D_{\textit{n}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐯</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(\mathbf{v}_{\textit{n}},z_{\textit{n}})\}_{i=1}^{D_{\textit{n}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, each local dataset <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\textit{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\textit{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> underscores the collaborative pursuit of model enhancement while steadfastly safeguarding data privacy concerns.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The system starts with local model training, in this process the computation frequency <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\textit{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\textit{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> of user <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> determines the time <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\textit{n}}^{\textit{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">train</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\textit{n}}^{\textit{train}}</annotation></semantics></math> required for processing data and the energy consumption <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\textit{n}}^{train}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\textit{n}}^{train}</annotation></semantics></math> for completing <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\textit{n}}D_{\textit{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\textit{n}}D_{\textit{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> CPU cycles at user <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</p>
<table id="S2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\textit{n}}^{train}=\alpha I_{\textit{n}}C_{\textit{n}}D_{\textit{n}}\phi_{\textit{n}}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\textit{n}}^{train}=\alpha I_{\textit{n}}C_{\textit{n}}D_{\textit{n}}\phi_{\textit{n}}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> is the effective capacitance coefficient.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">After local computations, each user uploads their local FL model using frequency domain multiple access (FDMA). In this step, the UAV communicates with terrestrial users primarily through Line-of-Sight (LoS) links. The power gain of the channel from the UAV to a user during the <math id="S2.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th time slot can be described by the free-space path loss model:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{UAV}[k]=\frac{\alpha_{0}}{d_{n,UAV}^{2}[k]}=\frac{\alpha_{0}}{x[k]^{2}+y[k]^{2}+H^{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{UAV}[k]=\frac{\alpha_{0}}{d_{n,UAV}^{2}[k]}=\frac{\alpha_{0}}{x[k]^{2}+y[k]^{2}+H^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the power gain at a reference distance <math id="S2.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math> meter, which is influenced by the carrier frequency and the antenna gains of both the transmitter and the receiver. Moreover, <math id="S2.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\textit{UAV, n}}[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV, n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\textit{UAV, n}}[k]</annotation></semantics></math> refers to the distance from the UAV to a terrestrial user at time slot <math id="S2.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, which is denoted by <math id="S2.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\textit{n, UAV}}[k]=\sqrt{x[k]^{2}+y[k]^{2}+H^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n, UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\textit{n, UAV}}[k]=\sqrt{x[k]^{2}+y[k]^{2}+H^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The users transmit power at time slot <math id="S2.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, represented as <math id="S2.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\textit{n}}[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\textit{n}}[k]</annotation></semantics></math>, is subject to both average and peak power constraints, denoted by <math id="S2.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\textit{peak}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">peak</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\textit{peak}}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively, i.e.,</p>
<table id="S2.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}p_{\textit{n}}[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}p_{\textit{n}}[k]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\bar{p}_{\textit{n}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">¯</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\bar{p}_{\textit{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{k=1}^{K}p_{\textit{n}}[k]\leq P_{\textit{n}},\quad\forall k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{k=1}^{K}p_{\textit{n}}[k]\leq P_{\textit{n}},\quad\forall k</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="S2.EGx3" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E6.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E6.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}p_{\textit{n}}[k]\leq\bar{p}_{\textit{n}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">¯</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{K}\sum_{k=1}^{K}p_{\textit{n}}[k]\leq\bar{p}_{\textit{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E6.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E6.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0\leq\sum_{k=1}^{K}p_{\textit{n}}[k]\leq P_{\textit{n}},\quad\forall k." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0\leq\sum_{k=1}^{K}p_{\textit{n}}[k]\leq P_{\textit{n}},\quad\forall k.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6b)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">To ensure these constraints are meaningful, it is assumed that <math id="S2.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{p}</annotation></semantics></math> is less than <math id="S2.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\textit{peak}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">peak</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\textit{peak}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Now we can calculate he uplink data rate <math id="S2.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\textit{up}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">up</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\textit{up}}</annotation></semantics></math> for user <math id="S2.SS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\textit{up}}_{\textit{n}}[k]=B\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\alpha_{0}p_{\textit{n}}[k]}{\sigma^{2}d_{\textit{n,UAV}}^{2}[k]}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">up</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n,UAV</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\textit{up}}_{\textit{n}}[k]=B\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\alpha_{0}p_{\textit{n}}[k]}{\sigma^{2}d_{\textit{n,UAV}}^{2}[k]}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> is bandwidth allocated to user (it is assumed bandwidth is equal to every user) and <math id="S2.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is the Additive White Gaussian Noise (AWGN) power. Similarly, the downlink data rate <math id="S2.SS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\textit{down}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">down</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\textit{down}}</annotation></semantics></math> for broadcasting the global model is given by</p>
<table id="S2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{\textit{down}}_{\textit{n}}[k]=B\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\alpha_{0}p_{\textit{UAV}}[k]}{\sigma^{2}d_{\textit{UAV, n}}^{2}[k]}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV, n</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{\textit{down}}_{\textit{n}}[k]=B\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\alpha_{0}p_{\textit{UAV}}[k]}{\sigma^{2}d_{\textit{UAV, n}}^{2}[k]}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p12.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\textit{UAV}}[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\textit{UAV}}[k]</annotation></semantics></math> is the UAV’s transmit power at time slot <math id="S2.SS2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">II-C</span> </span><span id="S2.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">DT Model</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">DT technology creates a detailed replica of physical systems, incorporating hardware setups, historical data, and real-time operational statuses. This functionality allows for seamless interaction with the physical system through mechanisms that enable real-time updates and control. The DT model for UAV-assisted FL can be defined as</p>
<table id="S2.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DT=(\mathcal{N},\mathcal{N}^{r}),(UAV,UAV^{r})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DT=(\mathcal{N},\mathcal{N}^{r}),(UAV,UAV^{r}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Digital replicas of the physical network, referred to as <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>r</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="UAV^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>r</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">UAV^{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, include all users and the UAV. By utilizing real-time updated data from physical entities, the digital services within DT layer provide a wide range of functionalities that enable autonomous management of the system.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The DT model <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DT_{\textit{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DT_{\textit{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>, employed for the local training process of the <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th user, can be expressed as <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="DT_{\textit{n}}=(\tilde{\phi}_{\textit{n}},\phi^{\prime}_{n})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">DT_{\textit{n}}=(\tilde{\phi}_{\textit{n}},\phi^{\prime}_{n}),</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\phi}_{\textit{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\phi}_{\textit{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the estimated processing rate of the physical user, and <math id="S2.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi^{\prime}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi^{\prime}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the deviation between the physical user and its DT model representation. The estimated time required to execute the task locally is given by</p>
<table id="S2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{T}_{\textit{n}}^{\textit{train}}=\frac{C_{\textit{n}}I_{\textit{n}}D_{\textit{n}}}{\tilde{\phi}_{\textit{n}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">train</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{T}_{\textit{n}}^{\textit{train}}=\frac{C_{\textit{n}}I_{\textit{n}}D_{\textit{n}}}{\tilde{\phi}_{\textit{n}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Assuming that the deviation between the physical user and its digital representation can be identified in advance, the latency gap for local model training can be calculated as follows:</p>
<table id="S2.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta T_{\textit{n}}^{\textit{train}}=\frac{C_{\textit{n}}I_{\textit{n}}D_{\textit{n}}\phi^{\prime}_{n}}{\tilde{\phi}_{\textit{n}}(\tilde{\phi}_{\textit{n}}-\phi^{\prime}_{n})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">train</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta T_{\textit{n}}^{\textit{train}}=\frac{C_{\textit{n}}I_{\textit{n}}D_{\textit{n}}\phi^{\prime}_{n}}{\tilde{\phi}_{\textit{n}}(\tilde{\phi}_{\textit{n}}-\phi^{\prime}_{n})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Hence we can write the actual time and energy uses for local model training as</p>
<table id="S2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\textit{n}}^{\textit{train}}=\tilde{T}_{\textit{Loc}}^{n}+\Delta T_{\textit{n}}^{\textit{train}}=\frac{C_{\textit{n}}I_{\textit{n}}D_{\textit{n}}}{\tilde{\phi}_{\textit{n}}-\phi^{\prime}_{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">train</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Loc</mtext><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">train</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\textit{n}}^{\textit{train}}=\tilde{T}_{\textit{Loc}}^{n}+\Delta T_{\textit{n}}^{\textit{train}}=\frac{C_{\textit{n}}I_{\textit{n}}D_{\textit{n}}}{\tilde{\phi}_{\textit{n}}-\phi^{\prime}_{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\textit{n}}^{train}=\alpha I_{\textit{n}}C_{\textit{n}}D_{\textit{n}}(\tilde{\phi}_{n}-\phi^{\prime}_{n})^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\textit{n}}^{train}=\alpha I_{\textit{n}}C_{\textit{n}}D_{\textit{n}}(\tilde{\phi}_{n}-\phi^{\prime}_{n})^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">II-C</span>1 </span>Local Model Uploading</h4>

<div id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The uploading power <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{DT}_{\textit{Pn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">DT</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Pn</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{DT}_{\textit{Pn}}</annotation></semantics></math> required for the local model upload from the <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-th user to the UAV can be expressed as <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{DT}_{\textit{Pn}}=(\tilde{p}_{\textit{n}},p^{\prime}_{\textit{n}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">DT</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Pn</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{DT}_{\textit{Pn}}=(\tilde{p}_{\textit{n}},p^{\prime}_{\textit{n}}),</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}_{\textit{n}}[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{\textit{n}}[k]</annotation></semantics></math> is the estimated power and <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}_{\textit{n}}[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}_{\textit{n}}[k]</annotation></semantics></math> represents the deviation between the physical system and its DTmodel. The estimated time to upload the local model, based on the DTmode estimation, is given by</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{T}_{\textit{n}}^{\textit{up}}[k]=\frac{D_{\textit{n}}}{R_{up}}=\frac{D_{\textit{n}}}{B\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\beta\tilde{p}_{\textit{n}}}{d_{\textit{n,UAV}}^{2}[k]}\right)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">up</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n,UAV</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{T}_{\textit{n}}^{\textit{up}}[k]=\frac{D_{\textit{n}}}{R_{up}}=\frac{D_{\textit{n}}}{B\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\beta\tilde{p}_{\textit{n}}}{d_{\textit{n,UAV}}^{2}[k]}\right)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{0}=\frac{\alpha_{0}}{\sigma^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{0}=\frac{\alpha_{0}}{\sigma^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. To incorporate the deviation <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}_{\textit{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}_{\textit{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the actual transmission power becomes <math id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}_{\textit{n}}-p^{\prime}_{\textit{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{\textit{n}}-p^{\prime}_{\textit{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the actual time to upload the local model is given by:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{up}}[k]=\frac{D_{\textit{n}}}{R_{up}}=\frac{D_{\textit{n}}}{B\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\beta_{0}(\tilde{p}_{\textit{n}}-p^{\prime}_{\textit{n}})}{d_{\textit{n,UAV}}^{2}[k]}\right)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">com</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">up</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n,UAV</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{up}}[k]=\frac{D_{\textit{n}}}{R_{up}}=\frac{D_{\textit{n}}}{B\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\beta_{0}(\tilde{p}_{\textit{n}}-p^{\prime}_{\textit{n}})}{d_{\textit{n,UAV}}^{2}[k]}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Thus we can write the actual energy consumption for local model uploading as</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{up}}[k]=(\tilde{p}_{\textit{n}}-p^{\prime}_{\textit{n}})\cdot T_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{up}}[k]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">com</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">up</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">com</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">up</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{up}}[k]=(\tilde{p}_{\textit{n}}-p^{\prime}_{\textit{n}})\cdot T_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{up}}[k].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">II-C</span>2 </span>Global model downloading</h4>

<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Transmit power associated with the UAV, denoted as <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{DT}_{p_{\textit{UAV}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">DT</mtext><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{DT}_{p_{\textit{UAV}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, plays a crucial role in the downloading process within the DT model representation, denoted by <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{DT}_{p_{\textit{UAV}}}=(\tilde{p}_{\textit{UAV}}[k],p^{\prime}_{\textit{UAV}}[k])," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">DT</mtext><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{DT}_{p_{\textit{UAV}}}=(\tilde{p}_{\textit{UAV}}[k],p^{\prime}_{\textit{UAV}}[k]),</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}_{\textit{UAV}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{\textit{UAV}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the estimated transmit power of UAV, while <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}_{\textit{UAV}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}_{\textit{UAV}}</annotation></semantics></math> signifies the divergence between the real UAV and its DT model counterpart. The estimated time for fetching the global model can be computed as</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{T}_{\textit{n}}^{\textit{down}}[k]=\frac{w_{\textit{n}}}{B\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\alpha_{0}\tilde{p}_{\textit{UAV}}[k]}{\sigma^{2}d_{\textit{UAV, n}}^{2}[k]}\right)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV, n</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{T}_{\textit{n}}^{\textit{down}}[k]=\frac{w_{\textit{n}}}{B\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\alpha_{0}\tilde{p}_{\textit{UAV}}[k]}{\sigma^{2}d_{\textit{UAV, n}}^{2}[k]}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To compensate for deviations in transmission power <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}_{\textit{UAV}}[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}_{\textit{UAV}}[k]</annotation></semantics></math>, the operational transmission power <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}_{\textit{UAV}}[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{\textit{UAV}}[k]</annotation></semantics></math> is adjusted accordingly:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{down}}[k]=\frac{w_{\textit{n}}}{B\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\alpha_{0}(\tilde{p}_{\textit{UAV}}[k]-p^{\prime}_{\textit{UAV}}[k])}{\sigma^{2}d_{\textit{UAV},n}^{2}[k]}\right)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">com</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{down}}[k]=\frac{w_{\textit{n}}}{B\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\alpha_{0}(\tilde{p}_{\textit{UAV}}[k]-p^{\prime}_{\textit{UAV}}[k])}{\sigma^{2}d_{\textit{UAV},n}^{2}[k]}\right)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{down}}[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">com</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{down}}[k]</annotation></semantics></math> represents the actual time required for retrieving the global model considering adjusted transmission power.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The actual energy consumption associated with retrieving the global model can be inferred as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{down}}[k]=(\tilde{p}_{\textit{UAV}}[k]-p^{\prime}_{\textit{UAV}}[k])\cdot T_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{down}}[k]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">com</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">com</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">down</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{down}}[k]=(\tilde{p}_{\textit{UAV}}[k]-p^{\prime}_{\textit{UAV}}[k])\cdot T_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{down}}[k].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS3.SSS3.6" class="ltx_text">II-C</span>3 </span>Total Latency and Energy Consumption</h4>

<div id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now we can calculate the total latency in DT for each global round is given by:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{n}^{total}=\max_{\forall n\in N}(T_{\textit{n}}^{\textit{train}}+T_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{up}}[k]+T_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{down}}[k])." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">train</mtext></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">com</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">up</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">com</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{n}^{total}=\max_{\forall n\in N}(T_{\textit{n}}^{\textit{train}}+T_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{up}}[k]+T_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{down}}[k]).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This equation computes the maximum total latency across all users in the system. It considers the local model training time <math id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\textit{n}}^{\textit{train}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">train</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\textit{n}}^{\textit{train}}</annotation></semantics></math>, uplink communication time <math id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\textit{com}}^{up}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">com</mtext><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\textit{com}}^{up}</annotation></semantics></math>, and downlink communication time <math id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\textit{com}}^{down}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">com</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\textit{com}}^{down}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">And the energy consumption is given by</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{n}^{total}=\sum_{n=1}^{N}(E_{\textit{n}}^{train}+E_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{up}}+E_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{down}}[k])." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">com</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">up</mtext></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">com</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{n}^{total}=\sum_{n=1}^{N}(E_{\textit{n}}^{train}+E_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{up}}+E_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{down}}[k]).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">This equation computes the total energy consumption for each user <math id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> in the system. It sums up the energy consumed during local model training <math id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\textit{n}}^{train}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\textit{n}}^{train}</annotation></semantics></math>, uplink communication <math id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\textit{com}}^{up}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">com</mtext><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\textit{com}}^{up}</annotation></semantics></math>, and downlink communication <math id="S2.SS3.SSS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\textit{com}}^{down}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">com</mtext><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\textit{com}}^{down}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS4.6" class="ltx_text">II-D</span> </span><span id="S2.SS4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Problem Formulation</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, the goal of the DT-assisted FL system is to minimize the energy consumption of the physical FL systems with the assistance of the DT. The problem can be formulated as follows<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="S2.EGx4" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E22.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E22.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\min_{\begin{subarray}{c}x[k],y[k],\\
\tilde{\Phi_{\textit{n}}},\tilde{p_{\textit{n}}},\tilde{p_{\textit{UAV}}[k]}\end{subarray}}\quad&amp;\sum_{n=1}^{N}\Bigg(\alpha I_{\textit{n}}C_{\textit{n}}D_{\textit{n}}(\tilde{\phi}_{n}-\phi^{\prime}_{n})^{2}\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{(\tilde{p}_{\textit{n}}-p^{\prime}_{\textit{n}})\cdot D_{\textit{n}}}{B\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\beta(\tilde{p}_{\textit{n}}-p^{\prime}_{\textit{n}})}{d_{\textit{n,UAV}}^{2}[k]}\right)}\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{(\tilde{p}_{\textit{UAV}}[k]-p^{\prime}_{\textit{UAV}}[k])\cdot w_{\textit{n}}}{B\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\alpha_{0}(\tilde{p}_{\textit{UAV}}[k]-p^{\prime}_{\textit{UAV}}[k])}{\sigma^{2}d_{\textit{UAV, n}}^{2}[k]}\right)}\Bigg)\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><munder><mi>min</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#000000">n</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#000000">n</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#000000">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n,UAV</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV, n</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\min_{\begin{subarray}{c}x[k],y[k],\\
\tilde{\Phi_{\textit{n}}},\tilde{p_{\textit{n}}},\tilde{p_{\textit{UAV}}[k]}\end{subarray}}\quad&amp;\sum_{n=1}^{N}\Bigg(\alpha I_{\textit{n}}C_{\textit{n}}D_{\textit{n}}(\tilde{\phi}_{n}-\phi^{\prime}_{n})^{2}\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{(\tilde{p}_{\textit{n}}-p^{\prime}_{\textit{n}})\cdot D_{\textit{n}}}{B\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\beta(\tilde{p}_{\textit{n}}-p^{\prime}_{\textit{n}})}{d_{\textit{n,UAV}}^{2}[k]}\right)}\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{(\tilde{p}_{\textit{UAV}}[k]-p^{\prime}_{\textit{UAV}}[k])\cdot w_{\textit{n}}}{B\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\alpha_{0}(\tilde{p}_{\textit{UAV}}[k]-p^{\prime}_{\textit{UAV}}[k])}{\sigma^{2}d_{\textit{UAV, n}}^{2}[k]}\right)}\Bigg)\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E22.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S2.E22.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_italic">s.t.</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E22.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0\leq\phi_{n}\leq\phi_{\textit{max}},\quad\forall n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0\leq\phi_{n}\leq\phi_{\textit{max}},\quad\forall n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22b)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E22.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E22.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0\leq p_{\textit{n}}\leq p_{\textit{max}},\quad\forall n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0\leq p_{\textit{n}}\leq p_{\textit{max}},\quad\forall n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22c)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E22.4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E22.4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0\leq p_{UAV}\leq p_{\textit{UAV, max}}[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV, max</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0\leq p_{UAV}\leq p_{\textit{UAV, max}}[k]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22d)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E22.5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E22.5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{n}^{total}\leq T_{\textit{max}},\quad\forall n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{n}^{total}\leq T_{\textit{max}},\quad\forall n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22e)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E22.6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E22.6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(x_{F}-x[K])^{2}+(y_{F}-y[K])^{2}\leq L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(x_{F}-x[K])^{2}+(y_{F}-y[K])^{2}\leq L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22f)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This problem incorporates constraints on bandwidth, computation frequency, upload power, download power, and latency for our system model. Constraint (<a href="#S2.E22.2" title="In 22 ‣ II-D Problem Formulation ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22b</span></a>) defines the permissible range for processing rate <math id="S2.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\textit{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\textit{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> for each user. Constraint (<a href="#S2.E22.3" title="In 22 ‣ II-D Problem Formulation ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22c</span></a>) limits the transmission power <math id="S2.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\textit{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\textit{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> for each user within the maximum power <math id="S2.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\textit{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\textit{max}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Constraint (<a href="#S2.E22.4" title="In 22 ‣ II-D Problem Formulation ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22d</span></a>) ensures the UAV’s transmission power <math id="S2.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{UAV}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{UAV}</annotation></semantics></math> does not exceed the maximum power <math id="S2.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\textit{UAV, max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV, max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\textit{UAV, max}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Constraint (<a href="#S2.E22.5" title="In 22 ‣ II-D Problem Formulation ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22e</span></a>) guarantees that the total time <math id="S2.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\textit{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\textit{n}}</annotation></semantics></math>, including local computation and communication times, does not surpass the maximum allowable time <math id="S2.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\textit{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\textit{max}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Constraint (<a href="#S2.E22.6" title="In 22 ‣ II-D Problem Formulation ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22f</span></a>) ensures that the final position of the UAV is within a permissible region defined by radius <math id="S2.SS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> centered at <math id="S2.SS4.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{F},y_{F})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{F},y_{F})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For our Problem, we assume simplified variables to manage complexity. First we assume the actual computation frequency of user in DT defined as <math id="S2.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\textit{n}}=\tilde{\phi}_{n}-\phi^{\prime}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\textit{n}}=\tilde{\phi}_{n}-\phi^{\prime}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly actual transmission power for user <math id="S2.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{n}[k]=\tilde{p}_{n}-p^{\prime}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{n}[k]=\tilde{p}_{n}-p^{\prime}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, and actual UAV’s transmission power, expressed as <math id="S2.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{UAV}[k]=\tilde{p}_{UAV}[k]-p^{\prime}_{UAV}[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{UAV}[k]=\tilde{p}_{UAV}[k]-p^{\prime}_{UAV}[k]</annotation></semantics></math>. The constants <math id="S2.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\frac{D_{n}}{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\frac{D_{n}}{B}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{w_{n}}{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{w_{n}}{B}</annotation></semantics></math> simplify bandwidth-related considerations for users and the UAV respectively. Now we can write the uapdated problem as,</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Problem 1:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="S2.EGx5" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E23.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E23.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\min_{\begin{subarray}{c}x[k],y[k],\\
f_{n},q_{n},q_{UAV}[k]\end{subarray}}\quad&amp;\sum_{n=1}^{N}\Bigg(\alpha I_{n}C_{n}D_{n}f_{n}^{2}\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{q_{n}\cdot\beta}{\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\beta q_{n}}{d_{n,UAV}^{2}[k]}\right)}\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{q_{UAV}[k]\cdot\gamma}{\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\alpha_{0}q_{UAV}[k]}{\sigma^{2}d_{UAV,n}^{2}[k]}\right)}\Bigg)\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><munder><mi>min</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\min_{\begin{subarray}{c}x[k],y[k],\\
f_{n},q_{n},q_{UAV}[k]\end{subarray}}\quad&amp;\sum_{n=1}^{N}\Bigg(\alpha I_{n}C_{n}D_{n}f_{n}^{2}\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{q_{n}\cdot\beta}{\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\beta q_{n}}{d_{n,UAV}^{2}[k]}\right)}\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{q_{UAV}[k]\cdot\gamma}{\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\alpha_{0}q_{UAV}[k]}{\sigma^{2}d_{UAV,n}^{2}[k]}\right)}\Bigg)\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E23.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S2.E23.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_italic">s.t.</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E23.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0\leq f_{n}\leq f_{\textit{max}},\quad\forall n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0\leq f_{n}\leq f_{\textit{max}},\quad\forall n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23b)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E23.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E23.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0\leq q_{n}\leq q_{\textit{max}},\quad\forall n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0\leq q_{n}\leq q_{\textit{max}},\quad\forall n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23c)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E23.4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E23.4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0\leq q_{UAV}[k]\leq q_{\textit{UAV, max}}[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV, max</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0\leq q_{UAV}[k]\leq q_{\textit{UAV, max}}[k]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23d)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E23.5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E23.5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{n}^{\text{total}}\leq T_{\textit{max}},\quad\forall n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi><mtext>total</mtext></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{n}^{\text{total}}\leq T_{\textit{max}},\quad\forall n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23e)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E23.6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E23.6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(x_{F}-x[K])^{2}+(y_{F}-y[K])^{2}\leq L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(x_{F}-x[K])^{2}+(y_{F}-y[K])^{2}\leq L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23f)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS5.6" class="ltx_text">II-E</span> </span><span id="S2.SS5.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proposed Solution</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It is evident that the objective function (<a href="#S2.E23.1" title="In 23 ‣ II-D Problem Formulation ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23a</span></a>) as well as the constraints (<a href="#S2.E23.5" title="In 23 ‣ II-D Problem Formulation ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23e</span></a>) and (<a href="#S2.E23.6" title="In 23 ‣ II-D Problem Formulation ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23f</span></a>) are non-convex. Due to the complexity of directly solving <span id="S2.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Problem 1</span>, we decompose it into two more manageable subproblems. Specifically, we divide the original problem into <span id="S2.SS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Subproblem 1</span>, which optimizes parameters for the users, and <span id="S2.SS5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Subproblem 2</span>, which focuses on optimizing the UAV parameters.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Subproblem 1:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="S2.EGx6" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E24.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E24.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\min_{\begin{subarray}{c}f_{\textit{n}},q_{\textit{n}}\end{subarray}}\quad&amp;\sum_{n=1}^{N}\Bigg(\alpha I_{n}C_{n}D_{n}f_{n}^{2}\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{q_{n}\cdot\beta}{\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\beta_{0}q_{n}}{d_{n,UAV}^{2}[k]}\right)}\\
&amp;\quad+E_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{down}}[k]\Bigg)\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><munder><mi>min</mi><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">com</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\min_{\begin{subarray}{c}f_{\textit{n}},q_{\textit{n}}\end{subarray}}\quad&amp;\sum_{n=1}^{N}\Bigg(\alpha I_{n}C_{n}D_{n}f_{n}^{2}\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{q_{n}\cdot\beta}{\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\beta_{0}q_{n}}{d_{n,UAV}^{2}[k]}\right)}\\
&amp;\quad+E_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{down}}[k]\Bigg)\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E24.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S2.E24.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_italic">s.t.</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E24.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0\leq f_{\textit{n}}\leq f_{\textit{max}},\quad\forall n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0\leq f_{\textit{n}}\leq f_{\textit{max}},\quad\forall n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24b)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E24.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E24.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0\leq q_{\textit{n}}\leq q_{\textit{max}},\quad\forall n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0\leq q_{\textit{n}}\leq q_{\textit{max}},\quad\forall n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24c)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E24.4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E24.4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle T_{n}^{total}\leq T_{\textit{max}},\quad\forall n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle T_{n}^{total}\leq T_{\textit{max}},\quad\forall n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24d)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">II-E</span>1 </span>Convexification of Sub-problem 1</h4>

<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Subproblem 1 is non-convex due to the objective function (<a href="#S2.E24.1" title="In 24 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24a</span></a>) and the constraint (<a href="#S2.E24.4" title="In 24 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24d</span></a>). In order to convexify (<a href="#S2.E24.1" title="In 24 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24a</span></a>), we introduce a slack variable <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\textit{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\textit{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="S2.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\textit{n}}\geq\frac{q_{\textit{n}}\beta}{\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{q_{\textit{n}}}{d_{\textit{n,UAV}}^{2}[k]}\right)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n,UAV</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\textit{n}}\geq\frac{q_{\textit{n}}\beta}{\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{q_{\textit{n}}}{d_{\textit{n,UAV}}^{2}[k]}\right)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Now we introduce more slack variables <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="S2.EGx7" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E26.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E26.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\psi z_{\textit{n}}\geq\beta q_{\textit{n}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\psi z_{\textit{n}}\geq\beta q_{\textit{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E26.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E26.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log_{2}(1+\theta)\geq\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log_{2}(1+\theta)\geq\psi</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26b)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E26.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E26.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{q_{\textit{n}}}{d_{\textit{n},UAV}^{2}[k]}\geq\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{q_{\textit{n}}}{d_{\textit{n},UAV}^{2}[k]}\geq\theta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26c)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Here we can see (<a href="#S2.E26.1" title="In 26 ‣ II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26a</span></a>) and (<a href="#S2.E26.2" title="In 26 ‣ II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26b</span></a>) are non-convex. We can covexify these using Taylor expansion and inequalities respectively,</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\textbf{\lx@text@underline{\eqref{eq:sub26a}:}}\quad\bm{\Rightarrow}\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow class="ltx_underline"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">(</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold"><a href="#S2.E26.1" title="In 26 ‣ II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_bold"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26a</span></a></mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">):</mtext></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textbf{\lx@text@underline{\eqref{eq:sub26a}:}}\quad\bm{\Rightarrow}\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\psi z_{\textit{n}}\geq\beta q_{\textit{n}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\psi z_{\textit{n}}\geq\beta q_{\textit{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\Rightarrow}\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\Rightarrow}\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{4}(z_{\textit{n}}+\psi)^{2}-\frac{1}{4}(z_{\textit{n}}-\psi)^{2}\geq\beta q_{\textit{n}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{4}(z_{\textit{n}}+\psi)^{2}-\frac{1}{4}(z_{\textit{n}}-\psi)^{2}\geq\beta q_{\textit{n}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\Rightarrow}\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\Rightarrow}\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{4}(z_{\textit{n}}+\psi)^{2}-\beta q_{\textit{n}}\geq\frac{1}{4}(z_{\textit{n}}-\psi)^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{4}(z_{\textit{n}}+\psi)^{2}-\beta q_{\textit{n}}\geq\frac{1}{4}(z_{\textit{n}}-\psi)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">In (<a href="#S2.E27" title="In II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>), the RHS is convex. For LHS, we can use the first order Taylor expansion:</p>
<table id="S2.E28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E28X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E28X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(z_{\textit{n}}+\psi)^{2}\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(z_{\textit{n}}+\psi)^{2}\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E28X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(z_{\textit{n(i)}}+\psi_{\textit{(i)}})^{2}+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n(i)</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(i)</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(z_{\textit{n(i)}}+\psi_{\textit{(i)}})^{2}+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E28Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E28Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2(z_{\textit{n(i)}}+\psi_{\textit{(i)}})(z_{\textit{n}}+\psi-z_{\textit{n(i)}}-\psi_{\textit{(i)}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n(i)</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(i)</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n(i)</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(i)</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2(z_{\textit{n(i)}}+\psi_{\textit{(i)}})(z_{\textit{n}}+\psi-z_{\textit{n(i)}}-\psi_{\textit{(i)}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p6.3" class="ltx_p">So we can rewrite (<a href="#S2.E28" title="In II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) as</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E29X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E29X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{4}[(z_{\textit{n(i)}}+\psi_{\textit{(i)}})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n(i)</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ψ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(i)</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{4}[(z_{\textit{n(i)}}+\psi_{\textit{(i)}})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E29X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+2(z_{\textit{n(i)}}+\psi_{\textit{(i)}})(z_{\textit{n}}+\psi-z_{\textit{n(i)}}-\psi_{\textit{(i)}})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n(i)</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ψ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(i)</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n(i)</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(i)</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+2(z_{\textit{n(i)}}+\psi_{\textit{(i)}})(z_{\textit{n}}+\psi-z_{\textit{n(i)}}-\psi_{\textit{(i)}})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E29Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E29Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\beta q_{\textit{n}}\geq\frac{1}{4}(z_{\textit{n}}-\psi)^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\beta q_{\textit{n}}\geq\frac{1}{4}(z_{\textit{n}}-\psi)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline ltx_font_bold">(<a href="#S2.E26.2" title="In 26 ‣ II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26b</span></a>):</span> Here we use the inequality to convexify:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex3X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex3X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ln(1+z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ln(1+z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex3X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\ln(1+z_{\textit{i}})+\frac{z_{\textit{i}}}{z_{\textit{i}+1}}-\frac{z_{\textit{i}}^{2}}{z_{\textit{i}+1}}\frac{1}{z}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">i</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">i</mtext></msub><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">i</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">i</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">i</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>z</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\ln(1+z_{\textit{i}})+\frac{z_{\textit{i}}}{z_{\textit{i}+1}}-\frac{z_{\textit{i}}^{2}}{z_{\textit{i}+1}}\frac{1}{z},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">thus the equation (<a href="#S2.E26.2" title="In 26 ‣ II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26b</span></a>) is approximated as follows:</p>
<table id="S2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ln(1+\theta_{\textit{i}})+\frac{\theta_{\textit{i}}}{\theta_{\textit{i}+1}}-\frac{\theta_{\textit{i}}^{2}}{\theta_{\textit{i}+1}}\frac{1}{\theta}\geq\psi\ln 2." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">i</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">i</mtext></msub><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">i</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">i</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">i</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ln(1+\theta_{\textit{i}})+\frac{\theta_{\textit{i}}}{\theta_{\textit{i}+1}}-\frac{\theta_{\textit{i}}^{2}}{\theta_{\textit{i}+1}}\frac{1}{\theta}\geq\psi\ln 2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline ltx_font_bold">(<a href="#S2.E26.3" title="In 26 ‣ II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26c</span></a>):</span> Equation (<a href="#S2.E26.3" title="In 26 ‣ II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26c</span></a>) is inherently convex, allowing for direct solution using CVX.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline ltx_font_bold">Convexify of constraints (<a href="#S2.E24.4" title="In 24 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24d</span></a>):</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E31X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E31X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow T_{n}^{\text{total}}\leq T_{\textit{max}},\forall n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi><mtext>total</mtext></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow T_{n}^{\text{total}}\leq T_{\textit{max}},\forall n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E31Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E31Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow T_{n}^{\text{train}}+T_{\text{com}}^{\text{up}}[k]+T_{\text{com}}^{\text{down}}[k]\leq T_{\textit{max}},\forall n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mi>n</mi><mtext>train</mtext></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>com</mtext><mtext>up</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>com</mtext><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow T_{n}^{\text{train}}+T_{\text{com}}^{\text{up}}[k]+T_{\text{com}}^{\text{down}}[k]\leq T_{\textit{max}},\forall n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E31Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E31Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow\frac{C_{n}I_{n}D_{n}}{f_{n}}+\frac{\beta}{\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\beta_{0}q_{n}}{d_{n,UAV}^{2}[k]}\right)}+T_{\text{com}}^{\text{down}}[k]\leq T_{\textit{max}},\forall n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>com</mtext><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow\frac{C_{n}I_{n}D_{n}}{f_{n}}+\frac{\beta}{\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\beta_{0}q_{n}}{d_{n,UAV}^{2}[k]}\right)}+T_{\text{com}}^{\text{down}}[k]\leq T_{\textit{max}},\forall n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p12.2" class="ltx_p">From (<a href="#S2.E31" title="In II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>) we can see that the first term of the LHS is convex, bout 2nd term is non-convex. Using slack varible <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\textit{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\textit{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> here we get</p>
<table id="S2.E32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E32X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E32X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{C_{n}I_{n}D_{n}}{f_{n}}+\frac{z_{\textit{n}}}{q_{\textit{n}}}+T_{\text{com}}^{\text{down}}[k]\leq T_{\textit{max}},\forall n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>T</mi><mtext>com</mtext><mtext>down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">max</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{C_{n}I_{n}D_{n}}{f_{n}}+\frac{z_{\textit{n}}}{q_{\textit{n}}}+T_{\text{com}}^{\text{down}}[k]\leq T_{\textit{max}},\forall n</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p12.3" class="ltx_p">To convexify the non-convex term in equation (<a href="#S2.E32" title="In II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>), we use the slack variable <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> as introduced previously. The term <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{z_{n}}{q_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{z_{n}}{q_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> needs to be convexified:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p">We can rewrite the term <math id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{z_{n}}{q_{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{z_{n}}{q_{n}}</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
<table id="S2.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{z_{n}}{q_{n}}\leq\frac{1}{4}\left(\left(z_{n}+\frac{1}{q_{n}}\right)^{2}-\left(z_{n}-\frac{1}{q_{n}}\right)^{2}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{z_{n}}{q_{n}}\leq\frac{1}{4}\left(\left(z_{n}+\frac{1}{q_{n}}\right)^{2}-\left(z_{n}-\frac{1}{q_{n}}\right)^{2}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p14.2" class="ltx_p">where 2nd quadratic term of the RHS is convex. Applying the first-order Taylor expansion for the 1st quadratic term as:</p>
<table id="S2.E34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E34X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E34X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(z_{n}+\frac{1}{q_{n}}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(z_{n}+\frac{1}{q_{n}}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E34X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(z_{n(i)}+\frac{1}{q_{n(i)}})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(z_{n(i)}+\frac{1}{q_{n(i)}})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E34Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E34Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+2(z_{n(i)}+\frac{1}{q_{n(i)}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+2(z_{n(i)}+\frac{1}{q_{n(i)}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E34Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E34Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(z_{n}+\frac{1}{q_{n}}-z_{n(i)}-\frac{1}{q_{n(i)}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(z_{n}+\frac{1}{q_{n}}-z_{n(i)}-\frac{1}{q_{n(i)}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<br class="ltx_break">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p14.3" class="ltx_p">Hence we can rewrite the subproblem 1 as follows:
<span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p14.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Reformulated Subproblem 1:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="S2.EGx10" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E35.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E35.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\min_{\begin{subarray}{c}f_{\textit{n}},q_{\textit{n}}\end{subarray}}\quad&amp;\sum_{n=1}^{N}\Bigg(\alpha I_{n}C_{n}D_{n}f_{n}^{2}+z_{\textit{n}}\ +E_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{down}}[k]\Bigg)\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><munder><mi>min</mi><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">com</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">down</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\min_{\begin{subarray}{c}f_{\textit{n}},q_{\textit{n}}\end{subarray}}\quad&amp;\sum_{n=1}^{N}\Bigg(\alpha I_{n}C_{n}D_{n}f_{n}^{2}+z_{\textit{n}}\ +E_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{down}}[k]\Bigg)\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E35.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S2.E35.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_italic">s.t.</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E35.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqref{eq:33},\eqref{eq:32},\eqref{eq:30},\eqref{eq:29},\eqref{eq:sub26c},\eqref{eqn:24a}-\eqref{eqn:24b}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#S2.E34" title="In II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#S2.E32" title="In II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#S2.E30" title="In II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#S2.E29" title="In II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#S2.E26.3" title="In 26 ‣ II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26c</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#S2.E24.2" title="In 24 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24b</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#S2.E24.3" title="In 24 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24c</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqref{eq:33},\eqref{eq:32},\eqref{eq:30},\eqref{eq:29},\eqref{eq:sub26c},\eqref{eqn:24a}-\eqref{eqn:24b}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35b)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<br class="ltx_break">
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Subproblem 2:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="S2.EGx11" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E36.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E36.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\min_{\begin{subarray}{c}x[k],y[k],q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]\end{subarray}}\quad&amp;\sum_{n=1}^{N}\Bigg(E_{\textit{n}}^{train}+E_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{up}}[k]\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{q_{UAV}[k]\cdot\gamma}{\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\alpha_{0}q_{UAV}[k]}{\sigma^{2}d_{UAV,n}^{2}[k]}\right)}\Bigg)\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><munder><mi>min</mi><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">com</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">up</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\min_{\begin{subarray}{c}x[k],y[k],q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]\end{subarray}}\quad&amp;\sum_{n=1}^{N}\Bigg(E_{\textit{n}}^{train}+E_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{up}}[k]\\
&amp;\quad+\frac{q_{UAV}[k]\cdot\gamma}{\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{\alpha_{0}q_{UAV}[k]}{\sigma^{2}d_{UAV,n}^{2}[k]}\right)}\Bigg)\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E36.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S2.E36.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_italic">s.t.</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E36.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0\leq q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]\leq q_{\textit{UAV, max}}[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV, max</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0\leq q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]\leq q_{\textit{UAV, max}}[k]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36b)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E36.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E36.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(x_{F}-x[K])^{2}+(y_{F}-y[K])^{2}\leq L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(x_{F}-x[K])^{2}+(y_{F}-y[K])^{2}\leq L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36c)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS5.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">II-E</span>2 </span>Convexification of Sub-problem 2</h4>

<div id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Subproblem 2 is non-convex due to the objective function (<a href="#S2.E36.1" title="In 36 ‣ II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36a</span></a>) and the constraint (<a href="#S2.E36.3" title="In 36 ‣ II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36c</span></a>). Similar to subproblem 1, we introduce a slack variable <math id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> to convexify (<a href="#S2.E36.1" title="In 36 ‣ II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36a</span></a>) as follows</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\geq\frac{q_{\textit{UAV}[k]}\gamma}{\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]}{\sigma^{2}d_{\textit{UAV, n}}^{2}[k]}\right)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV, n</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\geq\frac{q_{\textit{UAV}[k]}\gamma}{\log_{2}\left(1+\frac{q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]}{\sigma^{2}d_{\textit{UAV, n}}^{2}[k]}\right)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Subsequently, we introduce three more slack variables <math id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and equivalently re-write (<a href="#S2.E37" title="In II-E2 Convexification of Sub-problem 2 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>) as follows</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="S2.EGx12" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E38.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E38.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\xi\omega\geq\gamma q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\xi\omega\geq\gamma q_{\textit{UAV}}[k],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E38.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E38.2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log_{2}(1+\eta)\geq\xi," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log_{2}(1+\eta)\geq\xi,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38b)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E38.3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E38.3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]}{\Lambda}\geq\eta," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]}{\Lambda}\geq\eta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38c)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E38.4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E38.4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle d_{\textit{UAV, n}}^{2}[k]\leq\Lambda,\quad\forall k." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV, n</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle d_{\textit{UAV, n}}^{2}[k]\leq\Lambda,\quad\forall k.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38d)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Here we can see (<a href="#S2.E38.1" title="In 38 ‣ II-E2 Convexification of Sub-problem 2 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38a</span></a>), (<a href="#S2.E38.2" title="In 38 ‣ II-E2 Convexification of Sub-problem 2 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38b</span></a>) and (<a href="#S2.E38.3" title="In 38 ‣ II-E2 Convexification of Sub-problem 2 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38c</span></a>) are non-convex. So we need to convexify them.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex1a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex1a.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\textbf{\lx@text@underline{\eqref{eq:sub37a}:}}\quad\bm{\Rightarrow}\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow class="ltx_underline"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">(</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold"><a href="#S2.E38.1" title="In 38 ‣ II-E2 Convexification of Sub-problem 2 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_bold"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38a</span></a></mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">):</mtext></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\textbf{\lx@text@underline{\eqref{eq:sub37a}:}}\quad\bm{\Rightarrow}\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex1a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\xi\omega\geq\gamma q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\xi\omega\geq\gamma q_{\textit{UAV}}[k],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex2a"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex2a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\Rightarrow}\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\Rightarrow}\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex2a.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{4}(\omega+\xi)^{2}-\frac{1}{4}(\omega-\xi)^{2}\geq\gamma q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{4}(\omega+\xi)^{2}-\frac{1}{4}(\omega-\xi)^{2}\geq\gamma q_{\textit{UAV}}[k],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\Rightarrow}\quad" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\Rightarrow}\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{4}(\omega+\xi)^{2}-\gamma q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]\geq\frac{1}{4}(\omega-\xi)^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{4}(\omega+\xi)^{2}-\gamma q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]\geq\frac{1}{4}(\omega-\xi)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p">In (<a href="#S2.E39" title="In II-E2 Convexification of Sub-problem 2 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>), the RHS is convex. For LHS, simillar to (<a href="#S2.E26.1" title="In 26 ‣ II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26a</span></a>) we can use the first order Taylor expansion:</p>
<table id="S2.E40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E40X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E40X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\omega+\xi)^{2}\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\omega+\xi)^{2}\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E40X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\omega_{\textit{(i)}}+\xi_{\textit{(i)}})^{2}+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(i)</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(i)</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\omega_{\textit{(i)}}+\xi_{\textit{(i)}})^{2}+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E40Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E40Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2(\omega_{\textit{(i)}}+\xi_{\textit{(i)}})(\omega+\xi-\omega_{\textit{(i)}}-\xi_{\textit{(i)}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(i)</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(i)</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(i)</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(i)</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2(\omega_{\textit{(i)}}+\xi_{\textit{(i)}})(\omega+\xi-\omega_{\textit{(i)}}-\xi_{\textit{(i)}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">So we can rewrite (<a href="#S2.E39" title="In II-E2 Convexification of Sub-problem 2 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>) as</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S2.E41X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E41X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{4}[(\omega_{\textit{(i)}}+\xi_{\textit{(i)}})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(i)</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(i)</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{4}[(\omega_{\textit{(i)}}+\xi_{\textit{(i)}})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E41X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+2(\omega_{\textit{(i)}}+\xi_{\textit{(i)}})(\omega+\xi-\omega_{\textit{(i)}}-\xi_{\textit{(i)}})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(i)</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(i)</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(i)</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">(i)</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+2(\omega_{\textit{(i)}}+\xi_{\textit{(i)}})(\omega+\xi-\omega_{\textit{(i)}}-\xi_{\textit{(i)}})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E41Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E41Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\gamma q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]\geq\frac{1}{4}(\omega-\xi)^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\gamma q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]\geq\frac{1}{4}(\omega-\xi)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline ltx_font_bold">(<a href="#S2.E38.2" title="In 38 ‣ II-E2 Convexification of Sub-problem 2 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38b</span></a>):</span> Simillar to (<a href="#S2.E26.2" title="In 26 ‣ II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26b</span></a>), we use the inequality to convexify here:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex3a" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex3Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex3Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ln(1+\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ln(1+\omega)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex3Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\ln(1+\omega_{\textit{i}})+\frac{\omega_{\textit{i}}}{\omega_{\textit{i}+1}}-\frac{\omega_{\textit{i}}^{2}}{\omega_{\textit{i}+1}}\frac{1}{\omega}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">i</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>ω</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">i</mtext></msub><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">i</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>ω</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">i</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">i</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ω</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\ln(1+\omega_{\textit{i}})+\frac{\omega_{\textit{i}}}{\omega_{\textit{i}+1}}-\frac{\omega_{\textit{i}}^{2}}{\omega_{\textit{i}+1}}\frac{1}{\omega}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">hence we can approximate the equation (<a href="#S2.E38.2" title="In 38 ‣ II-E2 Convexification of Sub-problem 2 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38b</span></a>) as follows:</p>
<table id="S2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\ln(1+\eta_{\textit{i}})+\frac{\eta_{\textit{i}}}{\eta_{\textit{i}+1}}-\frac{\eta_{\textit{i}}^{2}}{\eta_{\textit{i}+1}}\frac{1}{\eta}\geq\xi\ln 2." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">i</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>η</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">i</mtext></msub><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">i</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">i</mtext><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>η</mi><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">i</mtext><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\ln(1+\eta_{\textit{i}})+\frac{\eta_{\textit{i}}}{\eta_{\textit{i}+1}}-\frac{\eta_{\textit{i}}^{2}}{\eta_{\textit{i}+1}}\frac{1}{\eta}\geq\xi\ln 2.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_underline ltx_font_bold">(<a href="#S2.E38.3" title="In 38 ‣ II-E2 Convexification of Sub-problem 2 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38c</span></a>):</span> Equation (<a href="#S2.E38.3" title="In 38 ‣ II-E2 Convexification of Sub-problem 2 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38c</span></a>) can be equivalently expressed as</p>
<table id="S2.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]\geq\eta\Lambda.\quad" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]\geq\eta\Lambda.\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p11.2" class="ltx_p">Assuming <math id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we utilize successive convex approximation to estimate the equation (<a href="#S2.E43" title="In II-E2 Convexification of Sub-problem 2 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>) as:</p>
<table id="S2.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\Lambda\leq\frac{1}{2}\frac{\Lambda_{i}}{\eta_{i}}\eta^{2}+\frac{1}{2}\frac{\eta_{i}}{\Lambda_{i}}\Lambda^{2},\quad" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\Lambda\leq\frac{1}{2}\frac{\Lambda_{i}}{\eta_{i}}\eta^{2}+\frac{1}{2}\frac{\eta_{i}}{\Lambda_{i}}\Lambda^{2},\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p11.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are the feasible points of <math id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> at iteration <math id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, (<a href="#S2.E43" title="In II-E2 Convexification of Sub-problem 2 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>) can be convexified as</p>
<table id="S2.E45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]\geq\frac{1}{2}\frac{\Lambda_{i}}{\eta_{i}}\eta^{2}+\frac{1}{2}\frac{\eta_{i}}{\Lambda_{i}}\Lambda^{2}.\quad" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]\geq\frac{1}{2}\frac{\Lambda_{i}}{\eta_{i}}\eta^{2}+\frac{1}{2}\frac{\eta_{i}}{\Lambda_{i}}\Lambda^{2}.\quad</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<br class="ltx_break">
</div>
<div id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Reformulated Subproblem 2:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody><tr id="S2.EGx15" class="ltx_eqn_row"><td class="ltx_eqn_cell" colspan="5"></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E46.1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td colspan="2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E46.1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\min_{\begin{subarray}{c}x[k],y[k],q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]\end{subarray}}\quad&amp;\sum_{n=1}^{N}\Bigg(E_{\textit{n}}^{train}+E_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{up}}[k]+\omega\Bigg)\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><munder><mi>min</mi><mtable><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">UAV</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">n</mtext><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">com</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">up</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\min_{\begin{subarray}{c}x[k],y[k],q_{\textit{UAV}}[k]\end{subarray}}\quad&amp;\sum_{n=1}^{N}\Bigg(E_{\textit{n}}^{train}+E_{\textit{com}}^{\textit{up}}[k]+\omega\Bigg)\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46a)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S2.E46.2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="S2.E46.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_italic">s.t.</span></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E46.2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\eqref{eq:44},\eqref{eq:41},\eqref{eq:40},\eqref{eq:sub37d},\eqref{eq:sub35a}-\eqref{eq:sub35b}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#S2.E45" title="In II-E2 Convexification of Sub-problem 2 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#S2.E42" title="In II-E2 Convexification of Sub-problem 2 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#S2.E41" title="In II-E2 Convexification of Sub-problem 2 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#S2.E38.4" title="In 38 ‣ II-E2 Convexification of Sub-problem 2 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38d</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#S2.E36.2" title="In 36 ‣ II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36b</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>(</mtext><mtext><a href="#S2.E36.3" title="In 36 ‣ II-E1 Convexification of Sub-problem 1 ‣ II-E Proposed Solution ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36c</span></a></mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\eqref{eq:44},\eqref{eq:41},\eqref{eq:40},\eqref{eq:sub37d},\eqref{eq:sub35a}-\eqref{eq:sub35b}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46b)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS5.SSS2.p12.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, the above problem is now a standard convex program and can be efficiently addressed by convex optimization solvers, e.g., CVX.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS6.6" class="ltx_text">II-F</span> </span><span id="S2.SS6.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proposed zkFed model</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">There has been a notable effort to incorporate ZKP algorithms into the FL process. ZKP is a cryptographic protocol that allows one party, the prover, to demonstrate the truth of a statement to another party, the <span id="S2.SS6.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">verifier</span>, without revealing any information other than the validity of the statement itself. Essentially, it enables the <span id="S2.SS6.p1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">prover</span> to confirm possession or knowledge of something to the <span id="S2.SS6.p1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">verifier</span> without exposing any sensitive information or the methods used to establish the proof. The ZKP algorithm ensures soundness, meaning there’s a high probability that any deceit by the <span id="S2.SS6.p1.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">prover</span> can be detected <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>. Additionally, it guarantees completeness, ensuring that if the statement is indeed true, the verifier will be convinced of its authenticity by the <span id="S2.SS6.p1.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">prover</span>.
<br class="ltx_break">There are three main types of ZKP, Interactive Zero Knowledge Proof (iZKP): This involves multiple rounds of interaction between the prover and the <span id="S2.SS6.p1.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">verifier</span>, gradually increasing the <span id="S2.SS6.p1.1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">verifier</span>’s confidence without revealing sensitive information. Non-interactive Zero-Knowledge Proof (NIZK): This is the <span id="S2.SS6.p1.1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">prover</span> generates a single proof that the <span id="S2.SS6.p1.1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">verifier</span> can independently verify, eliminating the need for continuous communication. Succinct Non-interactive Zero-Knowledge Proof (SNARK): This is a highly efficient variant of NIZK proof, enabling complex computations to be succinctly proven and verified without interaction.
FL is a ML approach where multiple decentralized clients (e.g., mobile devices or organizations) collaboratively train a model under the coordination of a central server without sharing their local data. This ensures data privacy and security <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>, <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">33</a>]</cite>. In Fig.<a href="#S2.F2" title="Fig. 2 ‣ II-F Proposed zkFed model ‣ II System Model ‣ Secure UAV-assisted Federated Learning: A Digital Twin-Driven Approach with Zero-Knowledge Proofs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, presents model is presented to ensure data privacy and integrity across a network of multiple users and an aggregator, a UAV. Each user (User 1 to User n) independently computes model weights <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> on their local data, encrypts these weights, and signs them before transmission to the UAV, which serves as the aggregator. This process protects the data from potential attackers, as illustrated. The UAV aggregates these encrypted weights to compute the encrypted sum <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Enc}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Enc</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Enc}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the encrypted global model, using homomorphic encryption that allows for operations on ciphertexts that yield an encrypted result corresponding to operations on plaintext. Alongside, the UAV constructs a zero-knowledge proof <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> that verifies the correctness of the encrypted computations without revealing any underlying data or weights, thereby ensuring the confidentiality and integrity of each user’s data. The equations <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=\sum\omega_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=\sum\omega_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Enc}(\omega)=\prod\text{Enc}(\omega_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Enc</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∏</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Enc</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Enc}(\omega)=\prod\text{Enc}(\omega_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> signify that the final model weights are the sum of individual weights and the encrypted total weights are the product of the individually encrypted weights, typical in schemes where multiplicative operations in the encrypted domain agree to additive operations in the plaintext domain <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">34</a>]</cite>.
Finally, the UAV broadcasts the encrypted global model and the zero-knowledge proof back to all users, allowing them to verify the integrity and correctness of the aggregation process independently.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The theoretical basis of ZKPs in FL lies in the cryptographic principles that allow the <span id="S2.SS6.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">prover</span> (client) to convince the <span id="S2.SS6.p2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">verifier</span> (server) of the truth of a statement without revealing any information beyond the statement’s validity. This is achieved through interactive protocols where the <span id="S2.SS6.p2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">prover</span> and <span id="S2.SS6.p2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">verifier</span> engage in a series of challenges and responses <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">29</a>]</cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.13634v1/zkFL_UAV_com.png" id="S2.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:314/225;" width="314" height="225" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S2.F2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fig. 2</span>: </span><span id="S2.F2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">zkFed model with ZKPs for secure FL. Users encrypt local model weights <math id="S2.F2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> before sending them to a UAV aggregator, which computes the encrypted sum <math id="S2.F2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Enc(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Enc(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math> via homomorphic encryption, ensuring security and integrity.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Using ZKPs in FL provides several benefits:
<span id="S2.SS6.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Privacy Preservation</span>: Ensures that the server does not learn the actual data of the clients.
<span id="S2.SS6.p3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Security</span>: Protects against malicious clients that might submit incorrect updates.
<span id="S2.SS6.p3.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Integrity Verification</span>: Allows the server to verify the correctness of local computations without accessing the raw data. </span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="S2.SS6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Algorithm 1</span> presented is a zkFed model. This algorithm is a secure FL process incorporating cryptography and zk-SNARKs. It is designed to ensure privacy and integrity of the data while facilitating collective model training across multiple clients without revealing individual contributions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">ZKP Setup:<span id="S2.SS6.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Before the federated process begins, a one-time setup is performed. The aggregation logic is defined as a circuit using a language like </span>Circom<span id="S2.SS6.p5.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">. The </span>Groth16<span id="S2.SS6.p5.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> protocol is then used to generate a </span>proving key (pk)<span id="S2.SS6.p5.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> and a </span>verifying key (vk)<span id="S2.SS6.p5.1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> based on this circuit and the </span>BN254<span id="S2.SS6.p5.1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> elliptic curve. The proving key is securely given to the aggregator, while the public verifying key is distributed to all clients.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Initialization:<span id="S2.SS6.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Each client generates a pair of public and private keys for digital signatures and shares their public key with other clients via a Public Key Infrastructure (PKI). The aggregator also generates a key pair for signing.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Local Training, Encrypting, and Signing:<span id="S2.SS6.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Each client trains a local model and obtains weights, <math id="S2.SS6.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. These weights are then encrypted using a homomorphic encryption scheme involving public parameters <math id="S2.SS6.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS6.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, and a random number <math id="S2.SS6.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. This ensures that the weights can be aggregated without revealing their actual values. Each client signs their encrypted weights with their private key and sends them to the aggregator.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Global Aggregation and ZKP Generation:<span id="S2.SS6.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The aggregator collects the encrypted weights and signatures from all clients. It computes the global model weights by summing the individual weights and aggregates the encrypted weights. The aggregator then signs the aggregated encrypted weights. Subsequently, the aggregator uses its  </span>proving key (pk)<span id="S2.SS6.p8.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">  to generate a zk-SNARK proof, <math id="S2.SS6.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>.  This proof, created using a function like </span>Groth16.Prove<span id="S2.SS6.p8.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">, mathematically attests that the aggregated ‘Enc(w)‘ is the correct product of all individual ‘Enc(<math id="S2.SS6.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>)‘ values (the witness), without revealing the individual components.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Global Model Transmission and Proof Broadcast:<span id="S2.SS6.p9.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The aggregator sends the aggregated weights, the encrypted aggregated weights, its signature, and the zk-SNARK proof <math id="S2.SS6.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> to all clients.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS6.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS6.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS6.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Verification:<span id="S2.SS6.p10.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Each client uses its copy of the  </span>verifying key (vk)<span id="S2.SS6.p10.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">  to check the integrity of the received proof <math id="S2.SS6.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>.  By running the efficient </span>Groth16.Verify<span id="S2.SS6.p10.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> function, the client can confirm that the aggregation was performed correctly according to the original circuit.  If the proof is valid, clients use the global model weights for further local training; otherwise, they raise an error or request retransmission. The federation process is thus protected by our proposed model from attackers who might attempt to disrupt the model training process or deduce specific client information from the shared weights. By using zk-SNARKs, the aggregator and all clients can confirm the integrity of the training process without having direct access to any private information.</span></span></p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Proposed zkFed Algorithm with ZKP</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Input:</span><span id="alg1.l1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> ZKP proving/verifying keys </span><math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\text{pk},\text{vk})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">pk</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">vk</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\text{pk},\text{vk})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, client and aggregator signing keys.
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            
</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">for</span><span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> each client </span><math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l3.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to </span><math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l3.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="alg1.l3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">do</span><span id="alg1.l3.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}\leftarrow\text{TrainLocalModel}()" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">TrainLocalModel</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}\leftarrow\text{TrainLocalModel}()</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}\leftarrow\text{GenerateRandomNumber}()" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">GenerateRandomNumber</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\leftarrow\text{GenerateRandomNumber}()</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l5.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
